</p>

<h3>2. Server log files</h3>
<p>
    The web server automatically stores technical logs when the site is accessed. This may include:
</p>
<ul>
    <li>IP address (shortened or anonymised if configured)</li>
    <li>Date and time of request</li>
    <li>Accessed URL</li>
    <li>Referrer and browser information</li>
</ul>
<p>
    Processing is based on Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR for technical operation and security. Logs are kept for a
    limited time and not used for profiling.
</p>

<h3>3. Search logs</h3>
<p>
    For debugging and monitoring, search requests generate internal entries containing the elements listed
    above. The query text itself is never stored. Only a hash of the query and the top result identifiers
    are kept. These logs are not shared with third parties.
</p>

<h3>4. Data about listed researchers</h3>
<p>
    This site displays professional information about economists. All of it stems from public
    sources: the RePEc Author Service, where the listed researchers registered and maintain their
    own profiles, and the public knowledge base Wikidata. Processing is based on Art. 6(1)(f)
    GDPR, the legitimate interest in making publicly self-published academic information searchable.
    No contact details beyond a self-published homepage are shown; email addresses, phone numbers
    and postal addresses from the source data are not stored.
</p>
<p>
    If you are listed here and want your data corrected or removed, email
    <a href="mailto:eduard.bruell@zew.de">eduard.bruell@zew.de</a>. Note that corrections to
    affiliations and publication lists are best made at the source
    (<a href="https://authors.repec.org">authors.repec.org</a>), and corrections to biographical
    details at Wikidata, so they do not reappear with the next data update.
</p>

<h3>5. Cookies and analytics</h3>
<p>
    The site uses only cookies required for essential functions such as saving searches. No analytics or
    third-party tracking tools are used.
</p>

<h3>6. Contact by email</h3>
<p>
    If you send an email, your message and contact details are processed to handle your request. The legal
    basis is Art. 6(1)(b) or Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR.
</p>

